# Socrates' reductio: if "better" just meant "stronger", the stronger slaves (and two men over one) would be better, which Callicles denies.
# The conclusion is only implicit in S3 ("if they are not the stronger"); I take it as the conclusion drawn.
atom	better_is_stronger	the better are the stronger
atom	slaves_stronger	Callicles' slaves are stronger than he is
atom	slaves_better	Callicles' slaves are better than he is
atom	many_stronger	two men are stronger than one
atom	two_better	two men are better than one
P1	S2	slaves_stronger	kind empirical
P2	S2	¬slaves_better
P3	S2	¬two_better
